WEBVTT

00:00:24.324 --> 00:00:25.916
Commander Chakotay.

00:00:25.959 --> 00:00:27.654
I understand
you wanted to see me.

00:00:27.694 --> 00:00:30.424
I'm told you are the officer
in charge of personnel,

00:00:30.463 --> 00:00:32.988
that you prepare
the... duty assignments.

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:34.625
Is that the correct phrase?

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:36.532
That's right.

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:40.903
I'm finding it... difficult
to spend so much time alone.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:43.238
I am unaccustomed to it.

00:00:43.276 --> 00:00:45.608
The hours do not pass quickly.

00:00:45.645 --> 00:00:47.237
I can understand that.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:48.304
How can we help?

00:00:48.348 --> 00:00:51.112
I've been considering
the matter carefully.

00:00:51.151 --> 00:00:53.449
I would like to request
a duty assignment.

00:00:53.486 --> 00:00:56.353
Did you have something
specific in mind?

00:00:56.389 --> 00:00:58.482
Yes.

00:01:00.226 --> 00:01:01.625
Now what?

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:05.388
There's been a rupture
in the coolant injector.

00:01:05.432 --> 00:01:06.399
I can see that!

00:01:06.433 --> 00:01:07.491
Why haven't you sealed it off?

00:01:07.534 --> 00:01:08.831
I'm attempting to do so.

00:01:12.739 --> 00:01:14.468
That's better.

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:17.203
Lieutenant, I have an idea.

00:01:17.243 --> 00:01:18.232
Perhaps it would be advisable

00:01:18.278 --> 00:01:19.575
to reconfigure
the coolant assembly.

00:01:19.612 --> 00:01:20.772
That would give us
greater control

00:01:20.814 --> 00:01:22.076
over the pressure valve
emissions.

00:01:22.115 --> 00:01:23.241
You're probably right.

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:25.717
And tomorrow, we can do it
first thing, but not today.

00:01:25.752 --> 00:01:26.912
I don't understand.

00:01:26.953 --> 00:01:28.318
Why wait till tomorrow
when today?

00:01:28.354 --> 00:01:30.413
Not today, Vorik.

00:01:33.193 --> 00:01:35.184
Good morning.

00:01:35.228 --> 00:01:37.128
Here's the helm control
evaluation you wanted.

00:01:37.163 --> 00:01:38.323
Thank you.

00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:41.600
We still on for dinner tonight?

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:43.397
I may have to work.
I'll let you know.

00:01:44.904 --> 00:01:46.997
Uh-huh. Okay.

00:01:47.107 --> 00:01:49.871
Have you decided if you're...

00:01:49.909 --> 00:01:51.570
if you're going through with it?

00:01:51.611 --> 00:01:52.839
I have

00:01:52.879 --> 00:01:55.279
and I'm not.

00:01:55.315 --> 00:01:57.340
Today hasn't started out
very well

00:01:57.383 --> 00:01:58.543
and the last thing I need

00:01:58.585 --> 00:02:01.019
is to get involved with
some obscure Klingon ritual.

00:02:01.087 --> 00:02:02.952
You were the one
who suggested it.

00:02:03.056 --> 00:02:03.954
I know.

00:02:04.057 --> 00:02:05.354
And for one sentimental minute,

00:02:05.391 --> 00:02:07.518
I thought that I might
actually go through with it,

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:08.720
but not anymore.

00:02:08.761 --> 00:02:09.887
Of course not.

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:11.863
Wouldn't want to get
too sentimental.

00:02:14.434 --> 00:02:15.958
I overslept this morning

00:02:16.035 --> 00:02:19.129
because I forgot to tell
the computer to wake me

00:02:19.172 --> 00:02:22.198
and then the acoustic inverter
in my sonic shower blew out.

00:02:22.242 --> 00:02:24.233
That'll make your hair
stand on end.

00:02:24.277 --> 00:02:25.471
So I didn't have time
for breakfast

00:02:25.512 --> 00:02:26.979
and when I got here,
two people were out sick

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:29.139
so I had to cancel
the fuel cell overhaul.

00:02:29.182 --> 00:02:31.548
And then an injector burst
for no apparent reason

00:02:31.584 --> 00:02:33.142
and started spewing
plasma coolant...

00:02:33.186 --> 00:02:34.744
Well, that's a run of bad luck
all right.

00:02:34.787 --> 00:02:36.982
So, I am in a bad mood,
and I know

00:02:37.056 --> 00:02:38.887
that I am being
a little bit testy.

00:02:38.925 --> 00:02:41.359
No. That's okay.

00:02:41.394 --> 00:02:43.624
Think about that dinner.

00:02:46.399 --> 00:02:47.889
Be careful.

00:02:51.104 --> 00:02:53.004
Something interesting
just happened.

00:02:53.039 --> 00:02:54.233
What's that?

00:02:54.274 --> 00:02:56.469
Seven of Nine requested
a duty assignment.

00:02:56.509 --> 00:02:57.567
Fascinating.

00:02:57.610 --> 00:02:59.510
She wants to work
in Engineering.

00:02:59.546 --> 00:03:00.513
What?

00:03:00.547 --> 00:03:02.276
The Borg use transwarp conduits

00:03:02.315 --> 00:03:04.545
to travel through space
faster than warp speed.

00:03:04.584 --> 00:03:05.949
If we could create
one of them...

00:03:06.019 --> 00:03:08.487
We don't know anything
about transwarp technology.

00:03:08.521 --> 00:03:10.455
Playing around with it
could be dangerous.

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:11.787
That's where Seven of Nine
comes in.

00:03:11.824 --> 00:03:13.451
She's offered to work with you.

00:03:13.493 --> 00:03:15.461
What do you think
her real motives are?

00:03:16.529 --> 00:03:17.655
She's having a tough time

00:03:17.697 --> 00:03:19.631
making the transition
from the collective.

00:03:19.666 --> 00:03:20.690
She wants something to do.

00:03:20.733 --> 00:03:24.134
I never thought of you
as naive, Chakotay.

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:26.730
Bottom line is,

00:03:26.773 --> 00:03:29.435
I don't want her working
in Engineering.

00:03:29.475 --> 00:03:31.705
The bottom line is,
I'm giving you an order

00:03:31.744 --> 00:03:34.008
and you're going
to follow it, Lieutenant.

00:03:36.649 --> 00:03:37.707
Whatever you say, sir.

00:05:31.896 --> 00:05:34.364
Seven of Nine,
you told me you wouldn't

00:05:34.399 --> 00:05:36.492
make any more attempts
to contact the Borg.

00:05:36.534 --> 00:05:38.695
And I want to believe
that's true.

00:05:38.737 --> 00:05:39.965
I assure you it is.

00:05:40.005 --> 00:05:41.267
I've decided not to post

00:05:41.306 --> 00:05:43.831
a security detail while
you're in Engineering,

00:05:43.875 --> 00:05:45.900
but you have to realize
there are rules.

00:05:45.944 --> 00:05:48.139
You'll be expected
to follow our protocols.

00:05:48.179 --> 00:05:50.113
You'll report directly
to Lieutenant Torres

00:05:50.148 --> 00:05:52.116
and obey any order
she gives you.

00:05:52.150 --> 00:05:53.139
I understand.

00:05:53.184 --> 00:05:54.549
One more thing...

00:05:54.586 --> 00:05:58.215
your designation,
"Seven of Nine"

00:05:58.256 --> 00:06:00.486
is a little cumbersome.

00:06:00.525 --> 00:06:01.753
Wouldn't you prefer

00:06:01.793 --> 00:06:04.387
to be called
by your given name, Annika?

00:06:04.429 --> 00:06:08.263
I have been Seven of Nine
for as long as I can remember.

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:10.927
All right.

00:06:11.002 --> 00:06:13.562
But maybe we could
streamline it a little.

00:06:13.605 --> 00:06:15.903
How would you feel about...

00:06:15.940 --> 00:06:16.929
"Seven"?

00:06:18.810 --> 00:06:21.210
Lmprecise...

00:06:21.246 --> 00:06:22.804
but acceptable.

00:06:22.847 --> 00:06:24.747
Tuvok to Captain Janeway.

00:06:24.783 --> 00:06:25.750
Yes, Tuvok?

00:06:25.784 --> 00:06:27.251
Please come to the Bridge.

00:06:27.285 --> 00:06:28.809
A ship is approaching.

00:06:37.195 --> 00:06:39.095
It's damaged, but functional.

00:06:39.130 --> 00:06:40.825
Energy emissions are so low

00:06:40.865 --> 00:06:43.561
it's probably not capable
of warp speed.

00:06:43.601 --> 00:06:45.967
Several dozen life signs aboard.

00:06:46.071 --> 00:06:47.834
We are being hailed, Captain.

00:06:47.872 --> 00:06:48.998
Open a channel.

00:06:50.008 --> 00:06:51.669
I'm Captain Kathryn Janeway

00:06:51.709 --> 00:06:53.870
of the Federation
Starship Voyager.

00:06:53.912 --> 00:06:56.176
I am Rahmin.

00:06:56.214 --> 00:06:58.648
My people are the Caatati.

00:06:58.683 --> 00:07:00.514
I apologize

00:07:00.552 --> 00:07:06.388
for our appearance
and the condition of our ship.

00:07:06.424 --> 00:07:09.882
Most of our people
were assimilated by the Borg

00:07:09.928 --> 00:07:12.328
over a year ago.

00:07:12.363 --> 00:07:15.196
We lost everything.

00:07:18.636 --> 00:07:20.467
How many of you escaped?

00:07:20.505 --> 00:07:24.271
A few thousand, on 30 ships...

00:07:24.309 --> 00:07:28.405
all that's left
from a planet of millions.

00:07:28.446 --> 00:07:29.743
I'm sorry.

00:07:29.781 --> 00:07:30.907
Captain...

00:07:30.949 --> 00:07:33.042
I want to assure you

00:07:33.084 --> 00:07:36.815
my people were once
proud and accomplished.

00:07:36.855 --> 00:07:38.789
I understand.

00:07:38.823 --> 00:07:41.656
It pains me to have to ask this,

00:07:41.693 --> 00:07:46.790
but I have 88 people
to care for on this vessel.

00:07:46.831 --> 00:07:49.891
We need food, medicines.

00:07:49.934 --> 00:07:53.028
Is there any way
you could help us?

00:07:54.239 --> 00:07:55.536
Of course.

00:07:55.573 --> 00:07:57.973
Send us a list of your needs
and we'll see what we can do.

00:07:58.076 --> 00:08:00.806
I'm deeply grateful.

00:08:00.845 --> 00:08:04.406
If it's not too much to ask,

00:08:04.449 --> 00:08:07.316
is there any way
you might also spare

00:08:07.352 --> 00:08:10.287
a small quantity
of thorium isotopes?

00:08:10.321 --> 00:08:14.553
Without them,
our systems can't function.

00:08:14.592 --> 00:08:16.116
I think we can arrange that.

00:08:16.161 --> 00:08:17.924
I'll speak to my engineer.

00:08:17.996 --> 00:08:24.697
You... can't imagine
what this means to us, Captain.

00:08:24.736 --> 00:08:27.102
Thank you.

00:08:40.151 --> 00:08:42.517
How are those thorium isotopes
coming, Vorik?

00:08:42.554 --> 00:08:43.919
I'll admit I'm having trouble

00:08:43.955 --> 00:08:45.616
controlling
the neutron absorption.

00:08:45.657 --> 00:08:48.558
Try increasing
the temperature of the plasma.

00:08:48.593 --> 00:08:50.959
Get the thorium to the Captain
as soon as it's ready.

00:08:50.995 --> 00:08:52.155
Of course.

00:08:53.164 --> 00:08:54.529
Tell me something...

00:08:54.566 --> 00:08:58.764
when you hear
about people like the Caatati,

00:08:58.803 --> 00:09:01.271
do you have
any feelings of remorse?

00:09:05.443 --> 00:09:06.808
No.

00:09:06.844 --> 00:09:09.108
That's it?

00:09:09.147 --> 00:09:10.273
Just "no"?

00:09:10.315 --> 00:09:13.250
What further answer
do you require?

00:09:13.284 --> 00:09:15.275
Oh, maybe some kind
of acknowledgment

00:09:15.320 --> 00:09:18.221
of the billions of lives
you helped destroy...

00:09:18.256 --> 00:09:20.486
a justification
for what you did...

00:09:20.525 --> 00:09:22.686
maybe...
a little sense of guilt.

00:09:22.727 --> 00:09:24.354
Guilt is irrelevant.

00:09:24.395 --> 00:09:26.659
Heartwarming.

00:09:26.698 --> 00:09:29.292
I've set the parameters
for the tachyon burst

00:09:29.334 --> 00:09:31.666
we'll need to create
a transwarp conduit.

00:09:33.571 --> 00:09:35.869
It will be several hours
before the main deflector

00:09:35.907 --> 00:09:37.431
can be modified.

00:09:37.475 --> 00:09:39.875
I think it would be best
if I waited in my alcove.

00:09:39.911 --> 00:09:42.277
I think you're right.

00:10:08.506 --> 00:10:09.939
If I ever saw

00:10:09.974 --> 00:10:12.704
a job for the morale officer,
it's sitting right here.

00:10:12.744 --> 00:10:14.507
I'll bet I can help.

00:10:14.545 --> 00:10:16.706
You're facing
a big challenge, Neelix.

00:10:16.748 --> 00:10:18.807
I enjoy a challenge.

00:10:21.653 --> 00:10:23.848
Is that supposed
to make me feel better?

00:10:23.888 --> 00:10:25.515
Blood pie, for the Day of Honor.

00:10:25.556 --> 00:10:27.490
How did you know about that?

00:10:27.525 --> 00:10:29.493
Has Tom been talking to you?

00:10:29.527 --> 00:10:31.222
Not at all.

00:10:31.262 --> 00:10:33.753
No, I-I make it a point
to know these things.

00:10:33.798 --> 00:10:35.823
And if I'm correct,

00:10:35.867 --> 00:10:37.732
many Klingon families
traditionally serve

00:10:37.769 --> 00:10:40.397
blood pie on the Day of Honor.

00:10:40.438 --> 00:10:43.464
I appreciate the gesture,
Neelix,

00:10:43.508 --> 00:10:47.239
but, um, I've decided to ignore
this particular tradition.

00:10:47.278 --> 00:10:50.577
No blood pie, no examining
my behavior over the last year

00:10:50.615 --> 00:10:52.913
to see if I measure up
to Klingon standards.

00:10:52.950 --> 00:10:54.645
Understood.

00:10:58.656 --> 00:11:00.214
Lieutenant...

00:11:03.528 --> 00:11:04.756
without knowing why

00:11:04.796 --> 00:11:07.765
there's a black cloud
hanging over your head,

00:11:07.799 --> 00:11:09.892
may I suggest something?

00:11:09.934 --> 00:11:11.526
Go right ahead.

00:11:11.569 --> 00:11:16.302
You have a... bit of a temper...

00:11:16.341 --> 00:11:18.434
that you keep reined in

00:11:18.476 --> 00:11:21.343
and sometimes,
it builds up inside you

00:11:21.379 --> 00:11:23.142
until you explode at someone.

00:11:24.215 --> 00:11:26.240
I'd say that about sums it up.

00:11:26.284 --> 00:11:29.082
I'm offering to be
a pressure valve.

00:11:30.188 --> 00:11:31.155
A what?

00:11:31.189 --> 00:11:35.353
You may use me
to blow off steam.

00:11:35.393 --> 00:11:36.917
When you're angry, come see me,

00:11:36.961 --> 00:11:37.928
call me names

00:11:37.962 --> 00:11:40.260
insult me,
question my parentage.

00:11:40.298 --> 00:11:41.788
I won't take it personally,

00:11:41.833 --> 00:11:43.858
and you won't need
to keep things

00:11:43.901 --> 00:11:44.890
bottled up inside anymore.

00:11:47.038 --> 00:11:50.906
That may be the nicest offer
I've had in a long time.

00:11:50.942 --> 00:11:53.604
Thank you, Neelix.

00:11:53.644 --> 00:11:57.478
You're sweet, but I'm not sure
I could do that to you.

00:11:57.515 --> 00:12:00.643
I'm here if you need me.

00:12:03.955 --> 00:12:04.944
Neelix...

00:12:07.191 --> 00:12:09.659
about this, um, Day of Honor.

00:12:10.728 --> 00:12:13.162
Do you think
I should go through with it?

00:12:14.832 --> 00:12:15.958
I've always thought

00:12:16.033 --> 00:12:17.898
traditions were good things...

00:12:17.935 --> 00:12:19.266
worth preserving.

00:12:20.972 --> 00:12:22.769
I've been thinking a lot
about...

00:12:22.807 --> 00:12:25.867
the rituals that my mother
taught me, and...

00:12:25.910 --> 00:12:30.438
they don't seem quite so hateful
as they did when I was a child.

00:12:30.481 --> 00:12:35.646
Maybe being so far away from
anything Klingon has changed me.

00:12:35.686 --> 00:12:38.655
It certainly can't hurt
to go through with the ceremony.

00:12:41.559 --> 00:12:44.221
I don't know
what effect it'll have on me.

00:12:46.097 --> 00:12:47.860
That's what's frightening.

00:12:54.972 --> 00:12:56.030
All right.

00:12:59.577 --> 00:13:00.874
Bring on the blood pie.

00:13:07.985 --> 00:13:09.452
I can do this.

00:13:28.806 --> 00:13:30.933
Qapla'!

00:13:30.975 --> 00:13:33.535
What warrior goes there?

00:13:33.577 --> 00:13:36.341
My name is B'Elanna.

00:13:36.380 --> 00:13:38.712
Have you come
to have your honor challenged?

00:13:38.749 --> 00:13:41.946
I guess so. Yes.

00:13:41.986 --> 00:13:45.422
Are you willing to see
the ceremony through to the end?

00:13:45.456 --> 00:13:47.720
That's the idea, isn't it?

00:13:47.758 --> 00:13:50.226
What do I do?

00:13:50.261 --> 00:13:52.729
It will be a lengthy ordeal.

00:13:52.763 --> 00:13:55.755
First, you must eat
from the heart

00:13:55.799 --> 00:13:57.733
of a sanctified targ.

00:14:05.643 --> 00:14:07.110
Pak lohr!

00:14:07.144 --> 00:14:11.410
Yes... the heart of a targ

00:14:11.448 --> 00:14:14.679
brings courage
to one who eats it.

00:14:14.718 --> 00:14:19.052
Next, you will drink mot'Ioch

00:14:19.089 --> 00:14:21.353
from the Grail of Kahless.

00:14:24.228 --> 00:14:27.561
Drink to the glory of Kahless,

00:14:27.598 --> 00:14:30.089
the greatest warrior
of all time.

00:14:35.806 --> 00:14:40.505
Kahless defeated his enemies
on the field of battle

00:14:40.544 --> 00:14:43.308
and built a mighty empire.

00:14:44.481 --> 00:14:47.109
How have you
proven yourself worthy?

00:14:47.151 --> 00:14:50.643
Um, I haven't built any empires,
and I can't say

00:14:50.688 --> 00:14:53.748
that I've personally defeated
any enemies in battle,

00:14:53.791 --> 00:14:56.089
but you have to realize,
I'm not living among warriors.

00:14:56.126 --> 00:14:58.651
Then how do you expect
to distinguish yourself?

00:14:58.696 --> 00:14:59.663
I don't know.

00:14:59.697 --> 00:15:02.165
I guess I'm doing
the best I can.

00:15:02.199 --> 00:15:05.100
Huh! A pitiful reply.

00:15:05.135 --> 00:15:07.433
Let us proceed.

00:15:07.471 --> 00:15:12.033
A warrior must endure
great hardship.

00:15:12.076 --> 00:15:14.567
To test your mettle,

00:15:14.611 --> 00:15:18.945
you will endure the Ritual
of Twenty Painstiks.

00:15:18.983 --> 00:15:21.884
After that,
you will engage in combat

00:15:21.919 --> 00:15:24.786
with a master of the bat'leth.

00:15:24.822 --> 00:15:29.885
Finally, you will traverse
the sulfur lagoons of Gorath.

00:15:31.061 --> 00:15:33.529
You know, I don't think so.

00:15:33.564 --> 00:15:36.294
I didn't want to do this
before you described it.

00:15:36.333 --> 00:15:37.823
Certainly not now.

00:15:37.868 --> 00:15:39.062
I'm leaving.

00:15:39.103 --> 00:15:42.869
Not until you have completed
the ceremony, pahtk.

00:16:06.230 --> 00:16:08.460
Thanks so much.

00:16:08.499 --> 00:16:09.989
It's been lovely.

00:16:20.511 --> 00:16:21.535
Come in.

00:16:25.783 --> 00:16:28.513
I tried to find you before,
but you were on the holodeck.

00:16:28.552 --> 00:16:30.452
That's right.

00:16:32.022 --> 00:16:34.217
You know, you left it running.

00:16:34.258 --> 00:16:37.716
There was a Klingon in there
who didn't look too happy.

00:16:37.761 --> 00:16:39.353
Really.

00:16:39.396 --> 00:16:42.229
Yeah, and he was nursing
a whale of a black eye.

00:16:42.266 --> 00:16:43.665
Looks like he had a run-in

00:16:43.700 --> 00:16:45.691
with someone having
a really bad day.

00:16:45.736 --> 00:16:47.670
That's very funny.

00:16:50.340 --> 00:16:51.807
So, how'd it go?

00:16:54.178 --> 00:16:56.646
It didn't.

00:16:56.680 --> 00:16:59.478
Do you mind if we talk
about something else?

00:17:01.418 --> 00:17:03.852
As a matter of fact, I do.

00:17:03.887 --> 00:17:06.788
You have been like
a spitting cobra all day

00:17:06.824 --> 00:17:08.485
and it's getting boring.

00:17:08.525 --> 00:17:11.016
You know, we designed that
holodeck program together,

00:17:11.061 --> 00:17:12.358
and I think you owe me
the courtesy

00:17:12.396 --> 00:17:13.454
of telling me what happened.

00:17:13.497 --> 00:17:17.365
It was ridiculous,
meaningless posturing.

00:17:17.401 --> 00:17:19.392
Honor, dishonor...
what does it matter?

00:17:19.436 --> 00:17:22.132
It matters because it's
part of who you are.

00:17:22.172 --> 00:17:25.198
You've been running away
from that your whole life.

00:17:25.242 --> 00:17:26.903
Who are you to tell me that?

00:17:28.545 --> 00:17:30.536
I care about you,

00:17:30.581 --> 00:17:32.640
but if you're going
to keep pushing me away,

00:17:32.683 --> 00:17:34.583
then there's no point
in my staying around, is there?

00:17:34.618 --> 00:17:36.677
Fine.
Just leave me alone.

00:17:36.720 --> 00:17:38.210
Oh, don't worry.

00:17:38.255 --> 00:17:39.847
If this is the way
you treat people

00:17:39.890 --> 00:17:42.450
who try to be your friend,
you'll be alone, all right.

00:17:58.809 --> 00:18:02.267
There are over 200 people
on our three ships alone.

00:18:02.312 --> 00:18:05.543
Every one of them
suffers from malnourishment,

00:18:05.582 --> 00:18:08.847
but it's been hardest
on the children.

00:18:08.886 --> 00:18:12.219
Every parent sacrifices
for their child,

00:18:12.256 --> 00:18:15.316
but even so,
there's not enough food.

00:18:15.359 --> 00:18:17.827
If you could hear
the crying of the babies,

00:18:17.861 --> 00:18:20.921
you would have as much trouble
sleeping at night as I do.

00:18:20.998 --> 00:18:23.330
Have you considered
relocation to a planet

00:18:23.367 --> 00:18:25.301
where you could
grow your own food?

00:18:25.335 --> 00:18:26.927
Of course...

00:18:26.970 --> 00:18:29.666
but we haven't
been welcomed anywhere.

00:18:29.706 --> 00:18:32.140
Because we have no resources,

00:18:32.176 --> 00:18:36.840
everyone treats us like
vagrants, even criminals.

00:18:36.880 --> 00:18:40.441
We're not unsympathetic,
but we have limited supplies.

00:18:40.484 --> 00:18:42.748
We can't possibly provide
enough for all your people.

00:18:42.786 --> 00:18:46.950
Forgive me, but, from my
perspective, you live in luxury.

00:18:47.024 --> 00:18:49.219
You don't suffer
from debilitating diseases.

00:18:49.259 --> 00:18:53.491
You have many sources
of energy... replicators.

00:18:53.530 --> 00:18:56.624
Your crew is very well fed.

00:18:56.667 --> 00:19:01.331
Apparently,
keeping your bellies full

00:19:01.371 --> 00:19:04.636
is more important to you than
helping those less fortunate.

00:19:04.675 --> 00:19:06.905
That's unfair.

00:19:06.977 --> 00:19:09.343
These are the most generous
people you could hope to meet,

00:19:09.379 --> 00:19:11.711
but if we gave supplies
to everyone who asked,

00:19:11.748 --> 00:19:13.340
we wouldn't have anything left.

00:19:13.383 --> 00:19:15.408
Neelix, how much food
can we spare?

00:19:17.421 --> 00:19:20.857
We could provide each ship
with several hundred kilograms.

00:19:20.891 --> 00:19:22.290
Do it and check with the Doctor

00:19:22.326 --> 00:19:24.385
to see if he can spare
any medical supplies.

00:19:25.963 --> 00:19:26.930
Aye, Captain.

00:19:26.964 --> 00:19:27.953
Thank you.

00:19:29.199 --> 00:19:33.135
May the gods smile
on you and your crew.

00:19:33.170 --> 00:19:37.300
Tuvok, please escort our guest
to the transporter room.

00:19:49.553 --> 00:19:51.612
I've never navigated
a transwarp conduit.

00:19:51.655 --> 00:19:53.384
Any problems
I should be aware of?

00:19:53.423 --> 00:19:55.948
You have no idea
what you're doing.

00:19:56.026 --> 00:19:58.620
If we attempt to enter one,
I'll have to take helm control.

00:19:58.662 --> 00:20:00.960
I am a quick study.

00:20:00.998 --> 00:20:02.727
What species is that?

00:20:02.766 --> 00:20:04.461
She is a human
who lived as a Borg.

00:20:04.501 --> 00:20:05.468
Borg!

00:20:05.502 --> 00:20:06.833
She is disconnected
from the collective.

00:20:06.870 --> 00:20:07.837
She won't harm you.

00:20:07.871 --> 00:20:09.532
Where's my wife?!
Where are my children?!

00:20:09.573 --> 00:20:11.370
What did you do with them
after you took them?!

00:20:11.408 --> 00:20:12.898
What did you do
with my family?!

00:20:12.943 --> 00:20:14.706
Mr. Paris, please proceed.

00:20:14.745 --> 00:20:18.681
I lost everything...
my family, my home!

00:20:18.715 --> 00:20:20.842
Sorry about that.

00:20:20.884 --> 00:20:22.181
About what?

00:20:22.219 --> 00:20:24.414
Well, the way he reacted to you.

00:20:24.454 --> 00:20:25.751
He didn't injure me.

00:20:25.789 --> 00:20:27.222
Good.

00:20:28.258 --> 00:20:30.226
There are
many people on this ship

00:20:30.260 --> 00:20:32.251
who have similar feelings
toward me.

00:20:33.797 --> 00:20:35.321
I'm afraid you're right.

00:20:35.365 --> 00:20:36.662
Does that bother you?

00:20:36.700 --> 00:20:38.167
No.

00:20:39.569 --> 00:20:42.197
Well, I'm not
one of those people.

00:20:42.239 --> 00:20:44.673
We all have a past.

00:20:44.708 --> 00:20:46.005
What matters is now.

00:20:46.043 --> 00:20:49.308
I'm uncertain
what you're trying to say.

00:20:49.346 --> 00:20:51.177
That...

00:20:51.214 --> 00:20:53.808
if there's any way
that I can help you

00:20:53.850 --> 00:20:56.011
adjust to your life
here on Voyager,

00:20:56.086 --> 00:20:57.815
please ask me.

00:20:57.854 --> 00:21:00.789
I will remember your offer.

00:21:18.341 --> 00:21:19.399
All systems are ready.

00:21:19.442 --> 00:21:20.704
We're only going to take a peek.

00:21:20.743 --> 00:21:23.735
We open a conduit, get
as much sensor data as we can,

00:21:23.780 --> 00:21:25.145
and then close it up.

00:21:25.181 --> 00:21:27.445
I want to take this
one step at a time.

00:21:27.483 --> 00:21:28.973
I've set up
a temporary tachyon matrix

00:21:29.051 --> 00:21:30.416
within the main deflector.

00:21:30.453 --> 00:21:31.545
It's on line.

00:21:31.587 --> 00:21:33.555
Engineering to the Bridge.

00:21:33.589 --> 00:21:34.954
We're ready to start, Captain.

00:21:34.991 --> 00:21:37.425
Go ahead. We'll monitor
your progress from here.

00:21:37.460 --> 00:21:38.984
We'll need to be at warp speed

00:21:39.061 --> 00:21:41.222
to create a large enough
subspace field.

00:21:41.264 --> 00:21:43.732
I'd like to reroute
helm control to Engineering.

00:21:43.766 --> 00:21:44.733
Agreed.
Janeway out.

00:21:44.767 --> 00:21:45.734
Take us past...

00:21:45.768 --> 00:21:47.360
Past warp 2. I know.

00:22:06.956 --> 00:22:08.856
We're at warp 2.3.

00:22:08.891 --> 00:22:10.119
All right.

00:22:10.159 --> 00:22:12.389
Vorik, start emitting
the tachyons.

00:22:12.428 --> 00:22:13.986
Energizing the matrix.

00:22:16.098 --> 00:22:18.589
There's no indication
of a subspace field.

00:22:18.634 --> 00:22:21.125
I'd recommend switching
to a higher energy band.

00:22:25.675 --> 00:22:27.575
That did something.

00:22:27.610 --> 00:22:28.838
The subspace field is forming.

00:22:33.549 --> 00:22:36.416
Tachyon particles are leaking
into the propulsion system!

00:22:36.452 --> 00:22:37.646
Shut down the deflector.

00:22:37.687 --> 00:22:40.622
Done, but the leak
is continuing.

00:22:42.625 --> 00:22:44.456
Janeway to Engineering.

00:22:44.493 --> 00:22:47.155
Tachyons are flooding
the warp core, Captain!

00:22:47.196 --> 00:22:49.391
If you can't stabilize
the core immediately,

00:22:49.432 --> 00:22:50.490
evacuate Engineering.

00:22:50.533 --> 00:22:53.127
Aye, Captain.
I'll get back to you.

00:22:53.169 --> 00:22:55.228
I've cut all power relays,
but the tachyon levels

00:22:55.271 --> 00:22:56.568
are still rising.

00:22:56.606 --> 00:22:58.767
All right. Everybody out!

00:22:58.808 --> 00:23:00.435
Now!

00:23:00.476 --> 00:23:01.443
That means you as well.

00:23:01.477 --> 00:23:02.569
I could be of help.

00:23:02.612 --> 00:23:03.909
That's an order!

00:23:06.949 --> 00:23:09.076
You can't order me.
I outrank you.

00:23:09.118 --> 00:23:11.348
We've got
to neutralize the core.

00:23:11.387 --> 00:23:14.686
I'll try decoupling
the dilithium matrix.

00:23:15.625 --> 00:23:16.853
No effect!

00:23:16.893 --> 00:23:18.258
Try it again.

00:23:20.029 --> 00:23:21.257
It's not working!

00:23:21.297 --> 00:23:22.491
The core's about to breach!

00:23:22.531 --> 00:23:24.158
I've got to try one more thing.

00:23:24.200 --> 00:23:26.065
B'Elanna, there's no time!

00:23:26.102 --> 00:23:27.296
We've got to get out of here!

00:23:29.906 --> 00:23:31.567
Come on!

00:23:31.607 --> 00:23:34.269
Computer, prepare
to eject the warp core

00:23:34.310 --> 00:23:37.905
Authorization:
Torres-omega-five-nine-three.

00:23:40.449 --> 00:23:43.714
Computer, eject the warp core.

00:23:53.029 --> 00:23:53.996
Torres to Janeway.

00:23:54.096 --> 00:23:54.994
Go ahead.

00:23:55.097 --> 00:23:57.622
We've dumped the core.

00:24:03.439 --> 00:24:05.703
Welcome to the worst day
of my life.

00:24:10.479 --> 00:24:11.946
Vorik, we have to get

00:24:11.981 --> 00:24:14.449
those impulse engines
back on line.

00:24:14.483 --> 00:24:15.575
You and Nicoletti get started.

00:24:15.618 --> 00:24:16.585
Yes, Lieutenant.

00:24:16.619 --> 00:24:17.881
Report.

00:24:17.920 --> 00:24:19.046
We're stopped dead.

00:24:19.088 --> 00:24:21.682
The warp core is millions
of kilometers away by now

00:24:21.724 --> 00:24:23.919
and the impulse engines
are seriously damaged.

00:24:23.960 --> 00:24:25.825
I can give you a few thrusters,
but that's about it.

00:24:25.861 --> 00:24:27.692
How long before I can
have impulse power?

00:24:27.730 --> 00:24:29.129
I can't give you
an estimate on that.

00:24:29.165 --> 00:24:30.427
We're still assessing
the damage.

00:24:31.934 --> 00:24:35.131
So much for opening
a transwarp conduit.

00:24:35.171 --> 00:24:38.572
I sent the Borg
back to her alcove.

00:24:38.607 --> 00:24:41.201
We won't be needing her
in here anymore.

00:24:41.243 --> 00:24:43.871
At least
the core's still intact.

00:24:43.913 --> 00:24:44.971
Tom.

00:24:45.047 --> 00:24:46.708
Take a shuttle and find it.

00:24:46.749 --> 00:24:48.546
See if you can tractor
it back to Voyager.

00:24:48.584 --> 00:24:49.573
Yes, ma'am.

00:24:49.618 --> 00:24:50.585
It'll be unstable.

00:24:50.619 --> 00:24:51.643
It should be repaired

00:24:51.687 --> 00:24:53.154
before he tries to put
a tractor beam on it.

00:24:53.189 --> 00:24:54.213
Well, then, you go with him.

00:24:54.256 --> 00:24:55.689
Do whatever you have to.

00:24:55.725 --> 00:24:57.124
Just get it back
here in one piece.

00:25:14.910 --> 00:25:17.845
We're getting near
some random ion turbulence.

00:25:17.880 --> 00:25:19.643
I'll change course to avoid it.

00:25:23.819 --> 00:25:25.946
I wonder what else
can go wrong today?

00:25:26.022 --> 00:25:29.389
If we get this core back,
I'm going right to bed

00:25:29.425 --> 00:25:30.949
and sleeping straight through
till tomorrow.

00:25:31.060 --> 00:25:32.789
Get this day over with.

00:25:32.828 --> 00:25:33.817
Well, look at it this way...

00:25:33.863 --> 00:25:34.955
how much worse could it get?

00:25:34.997 --> 00:25:36.487
Having to dump the warp core

00:25:36.532 --> 00:25:38.466
has to be the low point
of any day.

00:25:38.501 --> 00:25:40.901
Maybe it's me.

00:25:40.936 --> 00:25:45.066
Maybe I'm asking
for this trouble somehow.

00:25:45.107 --> 00:25:48.042
Or maybe it's just
a string of bad luck.

00:25:50.679 --> 00:25:53.546
Sensors have picked up
a polymetallic object.

00:25:53.582 --> 00:25:54.981
Could be the core.

00:25:55.051 --> 00:25:56.985
That's the warp signature,
all right,

00:25:57.053 --> 00:26:00.887
but there's something else
out there... a ship.

00:26:00.923 --> 00:26:02.914
According to sensors,
it has the same energy signature

00:26:02.992 --> 00:26:04.892
as the Caatati ships.

00:26:04.927 --> 00:26:06.918
Maybe they're guarding it
for us.

00:26:07.029 --> 00:26:09.122
Right.

00:26:12.368 --> 00:26:13.960
I see it.

00:26:15.404 --> 00:26:17.872
What do they think
they're doing?

00:26:17.907 --> 00:26:19.932
They're trying to put
a tractor beam on it.

00:26:20.042 --> 00:26:22.875
This is the Shuttle Cochrane
to the Caatati vessel.

00:26:22.912 --> 00:26:24.243
Please respond.

00:26:24.280 --> 00:26:26.145
Don't come any closer.

00:26:26.182 --> 00:26:28.309
We're performing
a salvage operation.

00:26:28.350 --> 00:26:30.511
Oh, what a coincidence...
so are we.

00:26:30.553 --> 00:26:32.180
I'm afraid we got here first.

00:26:32.221 --> 00:26:35.054
Don't interfere
or we'll open fire.

00:26:35.091 --> 00:26:38.117
Don't you realize
that core is highly unstable?

00:26:38.160 --> 00:26:39.650
If you try to tractor it
like that,

00:26:39.695 --> 00:26:41.822
you could cause
an antimatter explosion.

00:26:43.399 --> 00:26:45.162
They're not answering.

00:26:45.201 --> 00:26:46.566
Idiots!

00:26:46.602 --> 00:26:48.593
We have to stop them
from destroying the core.

00:26:48.637 --> 00:26:51.037
I'm going to try to disrupt
their tractor beam.

00:26:56.579 --> 00:26:58.137
It's working.

00:27:00.249 --> 00:27:01.739
What was that?

00:27:01.784 --> 00:27:04.878
They sent an antimatter pulse
back through our particle beam.

00:27:04.920 --> 00:27:06.012
Warning.

00:27:06.055 --> 00:27:08.546
Structural integrity field
has been compromised.

00:27:08.591 --> 00:27:11.025
Now at 53 percent and falling.

00:27:11.060 --> 00:27:14.052
Hull breach
in two minutes 20 seconds.

00:27:14.096 --> 00:27:15.927
Reroute power from the
propulsion and weapon systems.

00:27:17.032 --> 00:27:20.331
Warning. Hull breach in
two minutes, ten seconds.

00:27:20.369 --> 00:27:21.461
No effect.

00:27:23.606 --> 00:27:27.599
Warning. The structural
integrity field has collapsed.

00:27:27.643 --> 00:27:29.770
Hull breach in two minutes.

00:27:29.812 --> 00:27:32.212
We have to get out of here!

00:27:32.248 --> 00:27:35.843
Warning. Hull breach
in one minute, 50 seconds...

00:27:45.661 --> 00:27:48.653
Computer, send a distress call
to Voyager.

00:27:48.697 --> 00:27:49.686
Give them our coordinates.

00:27:51.700 --> 00:27:53.361
Computer, respond.

00:27:53.402 --> 00:27:55.529
The com systems must be down.

00:27:58.040 --> 00:28:00.270
Transporters are still on line.

00:28:00.309 --> 00:28:01.298
Stand by to energize.

00:28:05.714 --> 00:28:07.238
Energize.

00:28:31.071 --> 00:28:33.733
Paris to Voyager.

00:28:33.774 --> 00:28:35.867
Do you read me?

00:28:38.212 --> 00:28:40.442
Please respond.

00:28:40.481 --> 00:28:41.880
Paris to Voyager.

00:28:41.915 --> 00:28:43.109
It's no use.

00:28:43.150 --> 00:28:45.983
The com system in these suits
won't carry that far.

00:28:48.522 --> 00:28:51.252
When they get
the impulse engines repaired,

00:28:51.291 --> 00:28:53.054
they'll come looking for us.

00:28:53.093 --> 00:28:55.755
Well, I don't plan
on just drifting here,

00:28:55.796 --> 00:28:58.424
hoping somebody will come along
and rescue us.

00:28:58.465 --> 00:29:01.127
There must be something
we can do.

00:29:01.168 --> 00:29:02.726
Agreed.

00:29:05.172 --> 00:29:09.438
If we could interplex
the com systems in both suits,

00:29:09.476 --> 00:29:13.606
we might be able to create
a phased carrier wave.

00:29:13.647 --> 00:29:16.616
Voyager would read
the signature

00:29:16.650 --> 00:29:18.515
and know it's from us.

00:29:18.552 --> 00:29:20.019
Good idea.

00:29:20.053 --> 00:29:22.078
Let me access your controls.

00:29:23.724 --> 00:29:25.919
I thought you'd never ask.

00:29:34.868 --> 00:29:36.927
That's it.

00:29:47.881 --> 00:29:53.547
This would be a lot easier
if I had a hyperspanner.

00:29:53.587 --> 00:29:54.815
Hold still.

00:29:59.359 --> 00:30:01.759
Why is it we have
to get beamed into space

00:30:01.795 --> 00:30:03.820
in environmental suits

00:30:03.864 --> 00:30:07.960
before I can initiate
first contact procedures?

00:30:08.001 --> 00:30:12.165
Why is it that if we're alone
for more than 30 seconds,

00:30:12.206 --> 00:30:14.265
you start thinking
about contact?

00:30:14.308 --> 00:30:17.675
Oh. That is not fair.

00:30:17.711 --> 00:30:21.977
The other day in Engineering,
I must have gone...

00:30:22.082 --> 00:30:25.245
four minutes before I started
thinking about it.

00:30:26.687 --> 00:30:28.587
Okay...

00:30:28.622 --> 00:30:31.750
I'm ready to initiate
the carrier wave.

00:30:33.994 --> 00:30:35.018
Sorry.

00:30:37.764 --> 00:30:38.753
Better?

00:30:40.434 --> 00:30:41.992
Yeah.

00:30:42.102 --> 00:30:44.502
Let's hope
it's still that strong

00:30:44.538 --> 00:30:46.836
by the time
it gets to Voyager.

00:31:02.322 --> 00:31:03.619
Come in.

00:31:06.927 --> 00:31:09.555
Would you like tea or coffee?

00:31:09.596 --> 00:31:11.188
I have no need
to ingest liquids.

00:31:11.231 --> 00:31:13.358
I still receive energy
from the Borg alcove.

00:31:13.400 --> 00:31:14.367
My understanding is

00:31:14.401 --> 00:31:16.733
that you're almost ready
to begin eating food.

00:31:18.171 --> 00:31:20.696
That is what the Doctor says.

00:31:20.741 --> 00:31:22.368
Why have you asked me here?

00:31:22.409 --> 00:31:25.276
Whenever there's
an accident on the ship...

00:31:25.312 --> 00:31:27.780
even a minor one...
we investigate it

00:31:27.814 --> 00:31:30.977
in order to minimize the chances
of its happening again.

00:31:31.018 --> 00:31:32.508
A prudent course of action.

00:31:32.553 --> 00:31:34.578
I didn't have a chance
to talk to Lieutenant Torres

00:31:34.621 --> 00:31:35.610
before she left the ship,

00:31:35.656 --> 00:31:38.216
so... I wanted to ask you
some questions

00:31:38.258 --> 00:31:40.522
about what happened
in Engineering.

00:31:42.029 --> 00:31:43.860
Sensor logs indicate
that tachyons

00:31:43.897 --> 00:31:45.626
were leaking into the warp core.

00:31:45.666 --> 00:31:47.429
Do you have any idea
how it started?

00:31:47.467 --> 00:31:48.934
No.

00:31:48.969 --> 00:31:50.903
We had reconfigured
the deflector shield

00:31:50.938 --> 00:31:51.996
to emit tachyon bursts.

00:31:52.105 --> 00:31:54.096
The procedure
must've triggered the leak.

00:31:54.141 --> 00:31:56.109
Who was controlling
the tachyon bursts?

00:31:56.143 --> 00:31:57.508
Ensign Vorik.

00:31:57.544 --> 00:31:59.239
What were you doing?

00:31:59.279 --> 00:32:01.907
Monitoring the transwarp
frequencies.

00:32:01.949 --> 00:32:04.782
And did you at any time
access deflector control?

00:32:07.454 --> 00:32:09.922
You believe I'm responsible
for the accident,

00:32:09.957 --> 00:32:12.323
that I deliberately
sabotaged the ship.

00:32:12.359 --> 00:32:14.327
You're like the others.

00:32:14.361 --> 00:32:16.352
You see me as a threat.

00:32:19.633 --> 00:32:20.964
I won't lie to you.

00:32:21.001 --> 00:32:22.229
Part of me is suspicious.

00:32:22.269 --> 00:32:24.100
We've dealt
with tachyon fields before

00:32:24.137 --> 00:32:25.832
and never had
this kind of problem.

00:32:25.872 --> 00:32:28.966
Captain, I am unaccustomed
to deception.

00:32:29.076 --> 00:32:30.907
Among the Borg,
it was impossible.

00:32:30.944 --> 00:32:31.968
There were no lies,

00:32:32.045 --> 00:32:34.673
no secrets, and I assure you

00:32:34.715 --> 00:32:37.309
I had nothing to do with
the accident in Engineering.

00:32:46.326 --> 00:32:48.624
I believe you.
Thank you.

00:32:50.897 --> 00:32:53.889
I am finding it
a difficult challenge

00:32:53.934 --> 00:32:56.368
to integrate into this group.

00:32:56.403 --> 00:32:58.701
It is full
of complex social structures

00:32:58.739 --> 00:33:00.297
that are unfamiliar to me.

00:33:00.340 --> 00:33:01.466
Compared with the Borg,

00:33:01.508 --> 00:33:03.567
this crew is inefficient
and contentious.

00:33:05.178 --> 00:33:09.911
But it is capable of...
surprising acts of compassion.

00:33:09.950 --> 00:33:14.284
Unexpected acts of kindness
are common among our group.

00:33:14.321 --> 00:33:16.755
That's one of the ways
we define ourselves.

00:33:20.060 --> 00:33:21.527
Is there anything more?

00:33:21.561 --> 00:33:22.823
Yes.

00:33:22.863 --> 00:33:26.560
We still have to find out
what caused the tachyon leak.

00:33:26.600 --> 00:33:29.592
Tell me what you remember
about the power fluctuations

00:33:29.636 --> 00:33:31.103
in the propulsion system.

00:33:45.185 --> 00:33:47.415
This isn't anything
like the simulations

00:33:47.454 --> 00:33:49.046
we had at the Academy.

00:33:51.158 --> 00:33:53.285
They felt peaceful...

00:33:53.326 --> 00:33:56.261
like floating in the womb...

00:33:59.232 --> 00:34:01.530
but right now,

00:34:01.568 --> 00:34:04.696
I'm feeling a little sick
to my stomach.

00:34:06.239 --> 00:34:09.231
You dropped out too soon.

00:34:09.276 --> 00:34:10.868
In the third year,

00:34:10.911 --> 00:34:15.211
there's a six-week course
of actual space walks,

00:34:15.248 --> 00:34:17.546
so you can get used to them.

00:34:17.584 --> 00:34:20.951
I never would've lasted
to the third year.

00:34:21.054 --> 00:34:24.854
If I hadn't dropped out,
they would've asked me to leave.

00:34:26.493 --> 00:34:28.461
I wish I'd known you then.

00:34:28.495 --> 00:34:30.690
You'd have hated me.

00:34:30.731 --> 00:34:32.665
I can't imagine a time

00:34:32.699 --> 00:34:35.099
I wouldn't have
found you fascinating.

00:34:39.539 --> 00:34:41.473
What the hell was that?

00:34:42.909 --> 00:34:45.104
More ion turbulence.

00:34:45.145 --> 00:34:50.447
Warning. Oxygen level
at 114 millibars.

00:34:50.484 --> 00:34:53.510
My oxygen supply is leaking.

00:34:54.888 --> 00:34:58.289
Warning. Oxygen level
at 93 millibars.

00:34:58.325 --> 00:35:00.555
We'll have to share mine.

00:35:06.500 --> 00:35:08.934
Are you getting air now?

00:35:13.373 --> 00:35:14.533
Yes.

00:35:16.143 --> 00:35:18.236
Much better.

00:35:18.278 --> 00:35:19.870
Thanks.

00:35:21.281 --> 00:35:23.249
What's wrong?

00:35:23.283 --> 00:35:27.549
The turbulence must
have damaged my suit, too.

00:35:27.587 --> 00:35:30.920
I should have at least
24 hours worth of oxygen,

00:35:30.957 --> 00:35:33.653
but there's only about
a half hour left.

00:35:41.534 --> 00:35:43.365
Engineering to Captain Janeway.

00:35:43.403 --> 00:35:44.529
Yes, Ensign.

00:35:44.571 --> 00:35:45.560
I'm pleased to inform you

00:35:45.605 --> 00:35:47.072
that impulse power
should be restored

00:35:47.107 --> 00:35:48.301
within the hour.

00:35:48.341 --> 00:35:50.366
Good news. Let me know as soon
as the engines are on line.

00:35:50.410 --> 00:35:51.900
Yes, ma'am.

00:35:51.945 --> 00:35:55.278
Captain, I believe I've found
the cause of the accident...

00:35:55.315 --> 00:35:58.182
erratic fluctuations
in the ship's warp power.

00:35:58.218 --> 00:36:01.085
When tachyon levels rose
to a resonant frequency,

00:36:01.121 --> 00:36:02.554
core pressure increased.

00:36:02.589 --> 00:36:04.580
Then it was an accident.

00:36:05.825 --> 00:36:07.725
Come in.

00:36:07.761 --> 00:36:09.058
Captain, we've picked up

00:36:09.095 --> 00:36:11.256
a carrier wave
with a Starfleet signature.

00:36:11.297 --> 00:36:12.924
I'd guess it's Tom and B'Elanna,
but they're not

00:36:13.033 --> 00:36:13.931
answering our hails.

00:36:14.034 --> 00:36:14.932
They may be in trouble.

00:36:15.035 --> 00:36:16.297
As soon as we get
impulse power...

00:36:16.336 --> 00:36:19.066
Tuvok to the Captain.
Can you come to the Bridge?

00:36:19.105 --> 00:36:20.265
On my way.

00:36:25.145 --> 00:36:27.875
We're being approached
by an armada of Caatati ships.

00:36:27.914 --> 00:36:29.939
They're hailing us.

00:36:29.983 --> 00:36:31.644
On screen.

00:36:31.684 --> 00:36:33.151
Hello, Captain.

00:36:33.186 --> 00:36:35.347
You've brought some friends.

00:36:35.388 --> 00:36:36.855
Needy friends.

00:36:36.890 --> 00:36:40.189
We're hoping
you'll offer us more supplies.

00:36:40.226 --> 00:36:42.319
I made it clear last time
that we couldn't

00:36:42.362 --> 00:36:44.956
possibly provide you
with enough for all your ships.

00:36:45.031 --> 00:36:46.362
And I had to accept that

00:36:46.399 --> 00:36:49.232
because your ship
is more powerful than ours,

00:36:49.269 --> 00:36:51.260
but the situation has changed,
hasn't it?

00:36:51.304 --> 00:36:53.568
You seem to be
at a disadvantage now.

00:36:53.606 --> 00:36:55.767
We have your warp core.

00:36:55.809 --> 00:36:57.071
You can't escape.

00:36:57.110 --> 00:37:00.204
I'm hoping that will make you
more generous.

00:37:00.246 --> 00:37:03.044
We've given you
everything we can spare.

00:37:03.083 --> 00:37:05.643
Return the core,
and we'll be on our way.

00:37:05.685 --> 00:37:08.813
One of our ships might not seem
threatening to you,

00:37:08.855 --> 00:37:13.189
but I assure you, 27 can inflict
considerable damage.

00:37:13.226 --> 00:37:15.194
We are desperate.

00:37:15.228 --> 00:37:17.924
Prepare to send us food, weapons

00:37:17.997 --> 00:37:20.329
and your entire supply
of thorium.

00:37:20.366 --> 00:37:22.664
And that Borg
you're protecting...

00:37:22.702 --> 00:37:23.930
we want her, too.

00:37:24.003 --> 00:37:26.198
There are many
who would enjoy a chance

00:37:26.239 --> 00:37:28.673
to repay one of them
for what they did to us.

00:37:38.952 --> 00:37:42.080
I'm lowering the oxygen ratio.

00:37:42.122 --> 00:37:45.216
That should give us
a few more minutes.

00:37:45.258 --> 00:37:48.557
I'm feeling...

00:37:48.595 --> 00:37:50.563
kind of groggy.

00:37:50.597 --> 00:37:53.157
Oxygen deprivation.

00:37:53.199 --> 00:37:56.191
And you're lowering it?

00:37:56.236 --> 00:38:00.195
We have to try to make it
last as long as possible.

00:38:00.240 --> 00:38:03.403
It's ironic, isn't it?

00:38:04.811 --> 00:38:06.779
What?

00:38:06.813 --> 00:38:10.112
Today...

00:38:10.150 --> 00:38:13.745
the Day of Honor...

00:38:13.786 --> 00:38:17.586
is the day
that I'm going to die.

00:38:17.624 --> 00:38:20.388
We are not going to die.

00:38:20.426 --> 00:38:23.020
Would you stop
talking like that?

00:38:23.062 --> 00:38:25.690
We have to face up to it, Tom.

00:38:28.268 --> 00:38:31.066
There's something
I've been wanting to ask you.

00:38:31.104 --> 00:38:33.732
Well, now's the time.

00:38:35.475 --> 00:38:38.535
When we first met...

00:38:38.578 --> 00:38:42.446
you didn't have
a very high opinion of me.

00:38:42.482 --> 00:38:46.441
That's putting it mildly.

00:38:46.486 --> 00:38:52.618
I thought you were an arrogant,
self-absorbed pig.

00:38:54.394 --> 00:38:57.454
Flattery won't get you
any more oxygen.

00:39:01.100 --> 00:39:03.193
Do you think I've changed?

00:39:03.236 --> 00:39:04.430
A lot.

00:39:06.272 --> 00:39:09.571
Now you're a stubborn,
domineering pig.

00:39:13.313 --> 00:39:15.110
I'm just kidding.

00:39:18.751 --> 00:39:21.618
There I go again...

00:39:21.654 --> 00:39:24.088
just pushing you away.

00:39:28.661 --> 00:39:31.721
You were right about me.

00:39:31.764 --> 00:39:34.961
It's what I do...

00:39:37.704 --> 00:39:40.571
push people away.

00:39:40.607 --> 00:39:44.634
Well, it's a surefire way
of not getting hurt.

00:39:45.645 --> 00:39:47.306
What a coward I am.

00:39:49.048 --> 00:39:51.039
Shh...

00:40:11.237 --> 00:40:12.864
Our weapons are more
powerful than theirs.

00:40:12.905 --> 00:40:14.304
I say we fight.

00:40:14.340 --> 00:40:15.967
Maybe if we give them something.

00:40:16.075 --> 00:40:17.064
Like what?

00:40:17.109 --> 00:40:19.339
I can't imagine what
would satisfy them now.

00:40:19.378 --> 00:40:21.539
I will go.

00:40:21.580 --> 00:40:23.241
They asked for me.

00:40:23.282 --> 00:40:25.978
If I surrender myself,
perhaps they'll let you leave.

00:40:26.018 --> 00:40:27.315
That's very generous,

00:40:27.353 --> 00:40:29.150
but I will not turn
you over to them.

00:40:29.188 --> 00:40:30.553
I was only offering

00:40:30.589 --> 00:40:33.490
to do what would be best
for this group.

00:40:33.525 --> 00:40:34.924
You're part of this group now

00:40:34.960 --> 00:40:36.552
and we're going to protect you.

00:40:36.595 --> 00:40:37.926
It's time
to stop talking about this.

00:40:37.963 --> 00:40:39.988
Tom and B'Elanna are in trouble
and we have to find them.

00:40:40.065 --> 00:40:42.465
Tuvok, what's the status
of our weapons array?

00:40:42.501 --> 00:40:44.560
Weapons are
at the ready, Captain,

00:40:44.603 --> 00:40:46.628
but our shield strength
is extremely low.

00:40:46.672 --> 00:40:49.197
We'll have to shut down
nonessential systems.

00:40:49.241 --> 00:40:50.799
Reroute power to the shields.

00:40:50.843 --> 00:40:52.242
We're going to fight.

00:40:52.278 --> 00:40:53.836
That might not be necessary.

00:40:53.879 --> 00:40:57.713
Caatati technology is dependent
on thorium isotopes.

00:40:57.750 --> 00:40:59.809
If they had enough, they could
become self-sustaining.

00:40:59.852 --> 00:41:01.911
But we don't have
that much thorium to give them.

00:41:01.954 --> 00:41:03.546
When the Borg
assimilated the Caatati,

00:41:03.589 --> 00:41:06.683
the survivors lost their ability
to replicate the isotopes.

00:41:06.725 --> 00:41:08.283
But I have retained
that knowledge.

00:41:08.327 --> 00:41:11.558
I could design an energy matrix
that would produce

00:41:11.597 --> 00:41:13.121
thorium in large quantities.

00:41:13.165 --> 00:41:15.759
If you've had this knowledge all
along, why didn't you say so?

00:41:17.336 --> 00:41:20.066
I am not accustomed
to thinking that way.

00:41:20.105 --> 00:41:22.437
Borg do not consider
giving technology away,

00:41:22.474 --> 00:41:23.873
only assimilating it.

00:41:23.909 --> 00:41:27.174
And what do you suppose
made you consider it now?

00:41:29.281 --> 00:41:31.181
I am not certain.

00:41:31.216 --> 00:41:36.677
Maybe... it was just
an unexpected act of kindness.

00:41:38.257 --> 00:41:40.885
Work with Vorik
to build the energy matrix,

00:41:40.926 --> 00:41:42.120
while I convince the Caatati

00:41:42.161 --> 00:41:43.628
there's a better way
out of this.

00:41:48.934 --> 00:41:53.132
This matrix will produce
944 grams of thorium per day.

00:41:53.172 --> 00:41:54.730
Now you can power
all your systems

00:41:54.773 --> 00:41:58.231
and begin to rebuild
your replication technology.

00:41:58.277 --> 00:42:00.711
Will you allow us to leave?

00:42:00.746 --> 00:42:04.375
One device isn't enough
for all our ships.

00:42:04.416 --> 00:42:05.940
Using this matrix
as a template,

00:42:05.984 --> 00:42:08.179
you can construct
as many as you like.

00:42:08.220 --> 00:42:09.710
We can provide you
with components

00:42:09.755 --> 00:42:11.916
and specifications.

00:42:14.493 --> 00:42:16.256
You're free to go.

00:42:17.629 --> 00:42:19.620
And thank you.

00:42:20.799 --> 00:42:22.790
You're welcome.

00:42:39.885 --> 00:42:44.322
Warning. Oxygen level
at 104 millibars.

00:42:44.356 --> 00:42:46.950
Tom...

00:42:49.628 --> 00:42:50.595
Come on.

00:42:50.629 --> 00:42:53.257
Open your eyes.

00:42:53.298 --> 00:42:57.325
Warning. Oxygen level
at 87 millibars.

00:42:57.369 --> 00:43:00.429
I was having a dream.

00:43:00.472 --> 00:43:03.441
There's something I have to say.

00:43:03.475 --> 00:43:04.635
Me, too.

00:43:06.678 --> 00:43:10.375
I'm glad
the last thing I'll see is you.

00:43:10.416 --> 00:43:15.217
I've been a coward
about everything...

00:43:15.254 --> 00:43:18.951
everything that really matters.

00:43:19.057 --> 00:43:22.549
No. You're being
a little hard on yourself.

00:43:22.594 --> 00:43:24.061
No.

00:43:24.096 --> 00:43:26.530
I'm going to die...

00:43:26.565 --> 00:43:29.762
without a shred of honor,

00:43:29.802 --> 00:43:32.236
and for the first time
in my life,

00:43:32.271 --> 00:43:34.000
that really bothers me.

00:43:37.976 --> 00:43:40.410
So I have to tell you something.
I...

00:43:40.446 --> 00:43:45.213
Warning. Oxygen level
at 71 millibars.

00:43:48.420 --> 00:43:50.650
I have to tell you the truth.

00:43:52.291 --> 00:43:54.088
The truth about what?

00:44:00.365 --> 00:44:02.993
I love you.

00:44:06.972 --> 00:44:08.530
Say something.

00:44:12.644 --> 00:44:15.442
You picked a great time
to tell me.

00:44:45.344 --> 00:44:47.710
Voyager to Tom Paris.

00:44:47.746 --> 00:44:49.737
Tom, do you read me?
Respond.

00:44:54.386 --> 00:44:55.717
We're here.

00:44:55.754 --> 00:44:58.086
Prepare to beam aboard.
